# WebCut — assistant rules (applied to every edit)

Read ARCHITECTURE.md before editing. Enforce these on every change:

1. Dependency direction is one-way: ui/ → state/ → domain/. engine/,
   pipeline/, workers/ → domain/ only. domain/ imports nothing (pure TS, no
   React, no browser APIs). Never import React outside ui/.
2. Close every VideoFrame / AudioData / ImageBitmap in a finally block or
   immediately after use. Never store one in React state or a long-lived
   closure.
3. Timeline math is integer frames + RationalTime, never raw float seconds.
   Convert to seconds only at the encoder/decoder/audio boundary.
4. Playback is driven by the audio clock (AudioContext.currentTime); video
   re-derives which frame to show from it.
5. UI (.tsx) imports from state/ only — never pipeline/, workers/, engine/.
6. Drag/scrub updates transportStore preview state only during the gesture;
   commit to documentStore (one undo entry) on pointerup.
7. One module per change. If it needs more than one layer, stop and split.
